# Vault-DB skill activations (symlinks into ~/ai-os/skills/{claude,codex}).
# Activation is a machine-local transaction: these resolve only on the machine
# that has the vault, so tracking them would push dead links to every clone.
# The vault DB is the source of truth; re-activate with a symlink, never a copy
# (copies fork -- these did, and kept naming the pre-consolidation vault path).
.claude/skills/pickup
.claude/skills/wrapup
.claude/skills/lsat-lab-mega-set
.claude/skills/lsat-lab-transcribe
.claude/skills/lsat-u-architecture
.claude/skills/lsatu-cc-handoff
.claude/skills/shadcn
.agents/skills/pickup
.agents/skills/wrapup
.agents/skills/lsat-u-architecture
.agents/skills/lsatu-cc-handoff

# RC source bundle (build-time only, not shipped)
# Excluded by contents, not as a directory: git cannot re-include a path inside
# an excluded directory, and one file in here does need versioning.
scripts/rc-source/*
# The recovery pull is the exception. The rest of that directory is a 15MB
# vendor bundle re-extractable from its zip; this file is not — it is the 548
# RC questions pulled back from the LSAT Lab API, it is what makes every
# practice test complete, and at ~600KB it is worth keeping in the repo.
!scripts/rc-source/recovered/
scripts/rc-source/recovered/*
!scripts/rc-source/recovered/questions.ndjson
# questions.csv is the other exception, and for the same reason: at ~100KB it is
# the roster of what every RC section is SUPPOSED to contain, which is what lets
# audit-practice-tests.mjs see a missing tail rather than only an interior gap.
# Without it the audit silently degrades to a lower bound, so it ships.
!scripts/rc-source/data/
scripts/rc-source/data/*
!scripts/rc-source/data/questions.csv

# Python bytecode from the build scripts
scripts/__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/

# Local working snapshots taken before a destructive production action.
# Never pushed: these hold verbatim transcripts, including speech captured in
# the room by accident, which is exactly what some of them exist to delete.
.scratch/
.impeccable/review/

# Local Home design measurements and the separately built fixture preview.
.taste-skill/
dist-home-preview/
